# Integra AFC working agreement

Automated Fare Collection platform: one Django/DRF backend, three white-labeled
Angular 20 frontends. `CLAUDE.md` is the full source of truth for conventions —
read it before non-trivial work. Current phase status lives in
`docs/status-report-2026-08-14.md`.

## Process

1. **Spec before code.** Every phase/module gets `docs/specs/<phase>-<module>.md`
   (scope, data model, API surface, edge cases, failure modes, test plan,
   migration impact) before implementation starts. Template: `docs/specs/TEMPLATE.md`.
2. **ADRs for architectural decisions**, including options rejected and why —
   `docs/adr/`. Finalize a proposed ADR before spec'ing the phase that needs it,
   not during it.
3. **Thinnest vertical slice first**, then stop for review. Backend + frontend for
   one feature beats a complete backend with no consumer.
4. **Never guess on ambiguity.** Label unavoidable assumptions `ASSUMPTION:` in
   output rather than silently picking one.
5. **Self-check before declaring anything done** — `docs/self-check.md` defines
   "done" (backend tests, e2e, accessibility, security sweep, report format).
   Reports land at `docs/self-check-<date>.md`.

## Keeping docs current

`docs/architecture.md` (technical) and `docs/executive-overview.md`
(non-technical) are updated at the end of every phase/slice, not just at launch.
